  "lineage": "Sawt classical Arabian-Gulf urban-chamber song tradition of Bahrain and Kuwait, developed in eighteenth-nineteenth centuries through cultural and trade connections between Gulf merchant-class urban centers and Yemen (with Yemeni-Sanaani musical influence) and East Africa (Zanzibari merchant-class exchange). Performance configuration: male solo singer accompanying himself on oud, with mirwas small drum and hand-clapping from a small audience. Repertoire organizes around sawt arabi (longer, complex modal cycle) and sawt shami (shorter, lighter modal cycle).",
